From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH panvk-32attr 001] panvk: expose 32 vertex input attributes
Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: maxVertexInputAttributes/maxVertexInputBindings were pinned to the
 Vulkan minimum of 16 (MAX_VBS), which is our own bookkeeping limit: the Mali
 hardware supports up to 2^9 vertex attributes (see the comment above
 .maxVertexInputAttributes in panvk_vX_physical_device.c).  D3D11 - and
 therefore DXVK - needs 32 input elements, so games that use more than 16
 attributes could not create a pipeline.
 .
 Raise MAX_VBS (bindings + attribute table, including the duplicate in
 csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h) and MAX_VS_ATTRIBS (MALI_ATTRIBUTE slots reserved in
 the VS driver set, images follow them on pre-Valhall) to 32, and allow vertex
 shader input locations up to MAX_VS_ATTRIBS.  Widen
 pan_shader_info::attributes_read to 64 bits (it holds the NIR inputs_read
 mask, whose generic-attribute bits start at VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0 = 16, so
 locations 16-31 live above bit 31), which also makes the Bifrost
 attribute_count computation correct for sparse high locations.
 .
 Nothing is spoofed: the attribute descriptors are actually emitted for all
 32 locations on CSF (prepare_vs_driver_set loops over MAX_VS_ATTRIBS and
 vk_vertex_input_state supports 32 attributes), the limit reported to
 applications matches what the driver implements.
 .
 This patch is applied after the complete universal series
 (csf-v11 + jm-v9 + jm-v7) validated by upstream RC5-universal (v10 probes
 36/36-39/39 on Mali-G610/G710).  It is carried in its own family because
 csf-v11/092 has MAX_VS_ATTRIBS 16 as hunk context and would not apply after
 this change.
Source/Reference: Mesa 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b,
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h (MAX_VBS),
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h (duplicate MAX_VBS),
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_shader.h (MAX_VS_ATTRIBS),
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c (prepare_vs_driver_set),
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.h (attributes_read)
Tested GPU: none yet (compile-level)
Tested Kbase UAPI: n/a
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf-v11 + jm-v9 + jm-v7 (must be the last family applied)
Validation test: panvk-test vertex attribute stress with 32 locations

